{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "_readme": [
    "Every number under `thresholds` is PROVISIONAL configuration, not a measurement, until its entry says status=baseline.",
    "Provisional p95 budgets reuse the only budget that already exists in the repo: 500 ms (loadtests/smoke.js and the",
    "AghighHttpP95LatencyHigh alert rule) and 2000 ms for chat delivery (loadtests/chat-smoke.js DELIVERY_MS).",
    "Provisional error-rate budget = 1% (loadtests/smoke.js).",
    "After a baseline: set status to baseline, fill baseline.date (UTC, YYYY-MM-DD) and baseline.commit (git SHA of the",
    "run), and replace the numbers with ones derived from the 3-run median. See loadtests/README.md \"Calibration\".",
    "`assertions` are correctness conditions, not budgets: they are always enforced and never calibrated.",
    "Baseline budgets: p95 = 1.5 x the worst p95 of the recorded runs, rounded up (5 ms below 100, 50 ms below 1000, 500 ms above). Error-rate budgets stay at 1% (observed 0) except the naive variants. All numbers are for one laptop (6 cores / 12 threads, Windows 11 + WSL2, k6 on the same host) at the default loads in docs/benchmarks/; they are not capacity claims."
  ],
